      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine how many boxes can be fully repacked into boxes of 40 books each, and then find out how many books are left over after redistributing them.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of books in the warehouse:\n\n\\[\n1335 \\text{ boxes} \\times 39 \\text{ books/box} = 52165 \\text{ books}\n\\]\n\nNext, we find out how many full boxes of 40 books can be produced from 52165 books. We do this by dividing the total number of books by 40:\n\n\\[\n52165 \\div 40 = 1304 \\text{ full boxes} \\text{ with a remainder}\n\\]\n\nTo find the remainder, we are left with a number of books that, when added to 1304 boxes of 40 books each, does not exceed 52165. We calculate the remainder using the modulo operation:\n\n\\[\n52165 - (1304 \\times 40) = 52165 - 52160 = 5\n\\]\n\nThus, Melvin has \\(\\boxed{5}\\) books left over.",
