    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine how many of the original books are left over after repacking them into boxes with 40 books each, while also maximizing the number of boxes that can be filled.\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of books:**\n   The original chore sends 1335 boxes, each containing 39 books. \n   So, we calculate the total number of books mathematically:\n   \\[\n   1335 \\text{ boxes} \\times 39 \\text{ books per box} = 52315 \\text{ books}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the maximum number of boxes that can be fully repacked:**\n   After repacking, each box will contain 40 books. Therefore, Melvin needs to divide the total number of books by 40 to find out how many full boxes he can make:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{52315 \\text{ books}}{40 \\text{ books per box}} = 1307 \\text{ full boxes}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of books left over:**\n   To find out how many books are left over after filling these boxes, we check the remainder when we divide 52315 by 40:\n   \\[\n   52315 \\div 40 = 1307 \\text{ R } 35\n   \\]\n   The remainder here is 35, meaningafter packing the boxes, Melvin has 35 books left over.\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{35}\\)",
